        <untitled-ontology-57:Exam_Part>Motor</untitled-ontology-57:Exam_Part>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Stereotypic movement disorder is a condition in which a person makes repetitive, purposeless movements. These can be hand waving, body rocking, or head banging. The movements interfere with normal activity or may cause bodily harm.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
    </owl:Class>
    


